<section class="lunar-results" aria-labelledby="lunar-results-title" id="results">
  <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--plain">Results at a glance · DPS 2026</p>
  <h3 class="research-h3" id="lunar-results-title">
    Testing lunar interiors against independent observations.
  </h3>
  <p class="lunar-results-lede muted">
    The forward-model grid contains 1,425 interiors that match the Moon's mass. Additional observations narrow
    the possibilities and connect their internal structure to measurable tidal signals.
  </p>
  <ol class="lunar-findings">
    <li>
      <strong>19 interiors retained</strong><p>
        These also match the moment of inertia and core-radius constraints. Homogeneous, layered and FeO-rich
        mantles remain possible.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>GRAIL measurements within the model range</strong><p>
        The measured tidal response falls within the range predicted by the 19 interiors in all four degree-3
        orders.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Thermal geometry matters</strong><p>
        Across the 19 interiors, k<sub>3m</sub> varies by 2.5–2.8×. Where the mantle is warm matters more than thermal
        amplitude alone.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="lunar-result-figures">
    <figure>
      <h4>Which interiors remain?</h4>
      <img
        class="lunar-selection-light"
        src="/images/research/model-selection-light.svg"
        width="740"
        height="300"
        alt="19 of 1,425 interiors match mass, moment of inertia and core radius: 7 homogeneous, 5 layered and 7 FeO-rich mantles"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <img
        class="lunar-selection-dark"
        src="/images/research/model-selection-dark.svg"
        width="740"
        height="300"
        alt="19 of 1,425 interiors match mass, moment of inertia and core radius: 7 homogeneous, 5 layered and 7 FeO-rich mantles"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption>
        Mass, moment of inertia and core radius retain three mantle families: homogeneous, layered and
        FeO-rich. Counts from the DPS poster.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <h4>Predicted tides span the GRAIL measurements</h4>
      <a
        class="lunar-tidal-figure lunar-figure-light"
        href="/images/research/grail-tidal-response-light.svg"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        aria-label="Open the tidal-response comparison at full size"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/research/grail-tidal-response-light.svg"
          width="740"
          height="420"
          alt="Predictions from 19 elastic lunar interiors span the GRAIL measurements of k30, k31, k32 and k33; Park et al. error bars are 15 times the formal uncertainty"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </a>
      <a
        class="lunar-tidal-figure lunar-figure-dark"
        href="/images/research/grail-tidal-response-dark.svg"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        aria-label="Open the tidal-response comparison at full size"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/research/grail-tidal-response-dark.svg"
          width="740"
          height="420"
          alt="Predictions from 19 elastic lunar interiors span the GRAIL measurements of k30, k31, k32 and k33; Park et al. error bars are 15 times the formal uncertainty"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </a>
      <figcaption>
        The time-variable tide for the 2012 GRAIL orbit, redrawn from the original data behind panel 6.
        Overlap in each order does not establish a simultaneous fit by one interior.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <p class="lunar-results-scope muted">
    These results apply to the tested compositions and prescribed temperature fields. They do not identify a
    unique lunar interior: the Apollo-based seismic profiles remain unexplained, and the two interiors that
    match GRAIL's degree-1 structure do not also match the Apollo heat flow.
  </p>
  <div class="lunar-results-links">
    <a class="text-link" href="/files/posters/VELLARD_PosterDPS58.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
      >Read the DPS poster (PDF)</a
    >
  </div>
</section>

